    "sbar": {
      "situation": "The bank system has recovered after the incident commander reverted two bad pipeline config changes. The latest probe passes at every step.",
      "background": "About 14 s before the handover, the pipeline set payments max_transfer_minor from 1000000 to 1. About 12 s before, it set gateway balance_cache_ttl_s from 0.5 to 600.0.",
      "assessment": "With a limit of 1 minor unit, payments rejected almost every transfer ('422 amount exceeds transfer limit'), so the gateway refused requests. The 600 s balance cache would have shown stale balances, but this was hidden while payments were failing. The incident commander reverted payments max_transfer_minor to 1000000 and gateway balance_cache_ttl_s to 0.5, and both reverts succeeded; the last of 2 recovery checks, at 28 s, was clean.",
      "recommendation": "No further action is needed; keep watching the A1 and A2 refusal rates fall to 0%, as they are recent-window figures still draining rejects logged just before the revert. Operations should review the transfers rejected while the 1-minor-unit limit was in place."
    },
